, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "majority"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the largest part "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The majority of the population of Africa is under fifteen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you need to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "region"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In a region that is known to be hot and dry, surviving without water is impossible."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "independent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without being supervised"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It made them independent by having a water supply."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mock battle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a play fight"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can take a rest, and talk to their friends about the last mock battle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chief"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "head of the village"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can discuss what the chief had to say."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sharing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "experiencing together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Having them in different sizes means sharing the work! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le05ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Uses of the Gerund: Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a noun formed with a verb ending in <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>. <br/><br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Shopping</span> is fun.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Smoking</span> is a bad habit.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> can be used as the subject of the sentence. <br/><br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Living in small villages</span> is what they have always done. </span><br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Maintaining their own traditions and values</span> is what keeps them together and makes them unique. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> can also used as a complement of the verb \"<span class=\"italic\">to be</span>\". <br/><br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Vanessa is <span class=\"strong\">shopping</span>.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I am <span class=\"strong\">reading a book</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Traveling through the picturesque hills, stopping for a moment, you can hear the voices of children laughing and singing. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Surviving without water is impossible. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In Africa, they have just started using plastic buckets."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Having them in different sizes means sharing the work!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "People are no longer kept waiting in the sun to get water. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Gerunds</span> are used as adjectives when they describe something that causes an emotion. <br/><br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The movie is <span class=\"strong\">exciting</span>. </span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">This is an <span class=\"strong\">interesting</span> article</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Gerunds</span> are used after prepositions. <br/><br/>For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Richard is good at <span class=\"strong\">playing the guitar</span>. <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You should improve the text by <span class=\"strong\">adding connectors</span>.</span>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive Gerunds and Infinitives: Review"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the passive form of a gerund or infinitive to emphasize that the subject of the sentence is being acted upon.<br/>  If the subject of the sentence is the agent (the doer), you use an active sentence with an active gerund or infinitive.<br/>  If the subject is not the agent, we use a passive gerund or infinitive."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the following examples:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>They <span class=\"strong\">are required to bring</span> the from the wells. <br/> <li>The main job for the family <span class=\"strong\">are being done</span> by children.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here, the focus is on the receiver of the actions. The agent, or \u2018doer', of the action is not the focus. It is understood by the context of the writing that the \u2018doer' of the action are people and therefore not important. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Using passive forms of gerunds or infinitives adds variety and depth to your writing. This style of writing is used often in stories, articles and academic texts."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Children have now taken on the main jobs that need doing for the family."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They are required to bring the water from the wells. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This region is known to be hot and dry."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Water had to be carried over long distances in large heavy clay vats. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The vats needed to be put on women's heads to be carried over great distances to bring water home. Most families had only one vat, considered to be the most valuable household object."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm 10 things that you think could make a difference in people's lives if they had them?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write each item a piece of paper."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice saying how these items would change people's lives by focusing on the action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your 10 words with a partner and explain how these could help people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make sentences to go with your partner's words."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I think of 10 items that could make a difference in people's lives if they had them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice saying how these items would change people's lives, using gerunds and infinitives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my ideas with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"quest