rica is under fifteen. Children have now taken on the main jobs that need doing for the family. <br/>They are required to bring the water from the wells. In a region that is known to be hot and dry, surviving without water is impossible. What has recently made a big difference in getting the water? It's the simple modern plastic bucket.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le05ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "\"In Africa, they have just started using plastic buckets!\", you exclaim. \"Have these things we all use just arrived there?\"<br/> How can have they made things better?  Before the plastic bucket came to Africa, water had to be carried over long distances in large, heavy clay vats. <br/>The vats needed to be put on women's heads to be carried over great distances to bring water home. Most families had only one vat, considered to be the most valuable household object. It made them independent by having a water supply.", "id": 2, "time": "36000", "image": "engenn10le05ob11re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "The plastic bucket has changed how the African woman's life has been up to now. They're inexpensive. Having them in different sizes means sharing the work! <br/>The women are now free to do things. People are no longer kept waiting in the sun to get water. They can take a rest, and talk to their friends about the last mock battle or what the chief had to say.<br/>To many Africans, this small two dollar item is a miracle.", "id": 3, "time": "73000", "image": "engenn10le05ob11re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}